// secret — a value every renderer hides (R-secret-01, #4107), in pure Almide.
//
// `Secret[A]` is opaque: outside this module its field cannot be read and
// its record literal cannot be written (E033), so the only way in is
// `secret.new` and the only way out is a visible `secret.reveal`.
//
// The type's ONE declaration of how it prints is `Secret.repr` below. Every
// renderer reads it: interpolation, `println` of an enclosing record, list
// or option, the assert / abort failure block and the `almide test` report.
// They all print `Secret(***)`, whatever A is (R-secret-02).
//
// `==` on `Secret[String]` / `Secret[Bytes]` compares in constant time
// (`string.is_equal_constant_time` / `bytes.is_equal_constant_time`); for
// any other A it is E103 (R-secret-03). A Codec record derives `decode` for
// a `Secret` field and never derives `encode` (R-secret-04, E023).
/// A value that prints as `Secret(***)` everywhere; `secret.reveal` reads it.
mod type Secret[A] = { hidden: A }

/// x wrapped so that every renderer prints it as `Secret(***)`.
fn new[A](x: A) -> Secret[A] = { hidden: x }

/// The value s wraps.
fn reveal[A](s: Secret[A]) -> A = s.hidden

/// `Secret(***)`, for every A: the one form every renderer prints.
fn Secret.repr[A](s: Secret[A]) -> String = "Secret(***)"
